# Blazor Component Inheritance Style

When a component needs a custom base type, prefer an intermediate C# base class instead of placing a generic base type directly in the `.razor` file.

- Prefer `@inherits SomeComponentBase` in `.razor`.
- Define `SomeComponentBase` in C# and inherit from the generic/shared base there.
- Keep code-behind (`.razor.cs`) focused on page behavior, not generic inheritance plumbing.

Example:

- `ProductsBase : PagedListComponent<ProductResponse, ListProductQuery>` in `ProductsBase.cs`
- `@inherits ProductsBase` in `Products.razor`
